# Line-ending policy for T2AG
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# On 2026-08-06 a Windows tool rewrote 83 tracked files from LF to CRLF.
# `git diff HEAD` showed 83 files / ~25,000 lines changed; `git diff -w` showed
# zero. Nothing semantic had changed. Committing that would have poisoned
# `git log -S`, blame, and every piece of evidence bound to a file hash.
#
# This was a RECURRENCE. During the 0.2.2 campaign a `git clone` on Windows
# rewrote historical evidence files the same way and invalidated frozen
# manifest SHAs, which cost a full re-run of the exact-plan shadow.
#
# T2AG binds evidence to SHA-256 of file bytes (frozen plans, executor
# manifests, LessonPreparationSnapshot, receipt chains). Bytes therefore must
# not depend on which host performed the checkout. `eol=lf` is deliberate and
# stronger than `text=auto` alone: it pins the WORKING TREE, not just the blob,
# so a hash computed on Windows equals one computed anywhere else.
#
# Do not relax this to `text=auto` without `eol=lf`. Do not add `eol=crlf` for
# convenience: any file whose bytes are hashed must stay host-independent.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell entry points must be LF or they will not execute.
bin/t2ag        text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Delivered PowerShell is written ASCII-only and LF-safe on purpose; see
# tmp/clr0001/apply_clr0001_correction.ps1 for why (Windows PowerShell 5.1
# decodes .ps1 with the system ANSI codepage, so non-ASCII bytes corrupt the
# parse). Keep it LF like everything else.
*.ps1           text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never transformed, never diffed as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.exe           binary
*.dll           binary
*.traineddata   binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.docx          binary
*.pptx          binary
*.ttf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
